    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 1863.0272012570358,
      "text": "there is room for improvement in Latour's account of the Berlin key: \n\nfirst, at an empirical level due to the methods Latour used in the study and second, \n\nat a meta-conceptual level in its elevation of a priori arguments over situated stories. ",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 292.5736572692923,
      "height": 213,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 2133.052835698342,
      "text": "Annemarie Mol and Helen Verran that foreground the author as a reflexive participant, while distinguishing between the empirical component and the narrative element, offers a way for ANT theorists to assume responsibility for their accounts. We argue that this these approaches towards storytelling point the way towards more engaged, situated, and reflexive orientation for ANT in the 21st century",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 255,
