      "text": "Context of the Paper",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 152.4130859375,
      "height": 45,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 200,
        "b": 140
      }
    },
    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 1490.9759323744238,
      "text": "Latour dead time to review what ANT is. Why does this matter? Because we are defining the future of ANT. ",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 280,
      "height": 87,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 1645.5015668157298,
      "text": "Other special issues that have been created. Lots of focus on recent work\n\nBut little examinations of Latours early texts that have more to tell us about the fundmental nature of ANT",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 254.91469055521088,
      "height": 150,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 1357.4502979331178,
      "text": "Key important paper cited by man in fields beyond ANT, design archeology, became iconic for defining materility",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 228.68601791640822,
      "height": 108,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": 3.1368907820952643,
      "y": 2112.6272399956783,
      "text": "Latour’s Counter‑Moves\nTruth = transformation through mediation  \n Myth/parable = necessary vehicle of truth\nInterpretation = condition of truth’s survival\nGoal = restore narrative as ontological operator  ",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 334.65013005551873,
      "height": 129,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": 3.1368907820952643,
      "y": 2363.336255117131,
      "text": "A. Parable as Method\nIndirect, transformative speech \nProduces metanoia (shift in stance)\nRejects “Double Click” immediacy\n\nB. Maquette / Model-in-Scale\nSmall narrative = ontological laboratory\nExample performs theory, not illustrates it\n\nReprise (Repetition-with-Difference)\nTruth renewed through retelling\nParallel to Gospel multiplicity ",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 316.8888377874751,
      "height": 276,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": 3.1368907820952643,
      "y": 1935.4182248742259,
      "text": "Bultmann’s Key Commitments\nTruth = existential decision (kerygma) \nMyth = historically contingent shell\nInterpretation = extraction of core message \nGoal = “demythologize” to reach pure proclamation",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 377.00398084854567,
      "height": 129,
      "backgroundColor": {
        "r": 255,
        "g": 255,
        "b": 255
      }
    },
    {
      "x": -1543.4564462775313,
      "y": 1249.533416028857,
      "text": "Introduction",
      "imageUrl": null,
      "width": 150,
      "height": 45,
      "backgroundColor": {
